        "original_id": "ec5d5932-0bc1-52d2-94c3-4f0960d1148b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gregg Wager, Morten Lauridsen, Morton Subotnick\n- Places: Adrian, Michigan\n- Roles: composer, pianist, music critic, teacher, professor, composer-in-residence\n- Organizations: Los Angeles Master Chorale, University of Southern California Thornton School of Music\n- Awards: National Medal of Arts\n\nFacts:\n- Morten Johannes Lauridsen was born on February 27, 1943, and he is an American composer.\n- Gregg Wager was born on September 16, 1958, in Adrian, Michigan, and he is an American composer, pianist, and music critic.\n- Morten Lauridsen was composer-in-residence of the Los Angeles Master Chorale from 1994 to 2001.\n- Morten Lauridsen received the National Medal of Arts in 2007.\n- Morten Lauridsen has been a professor of composition at the University of Southern California Thornton School of Music for more than 40 years.\n- Gregg Wager's teachers included Morton Subotnick and Morten Lauridsen.",
